From the heads:  
\[ c + d = 180 \quad \text{(1)} \]  

From the bumps:  
Camels have 2 bumps each, and dromedaries have 1 bump each, so:  
\[ 2c + d = 304 \quad \text{(2)} \]  

Subtract equation (1) from equation (2):  
\[ (2c + d) - (c + d) = 304 - 180 \]  
\[ c = 124 \]  

Now substitute \( c = 124 \) into equation (1):  
\[ 124 + d = 180 \]  
\[ d = 180 - 124 \]  
\[ d = 56 \]  

There are **56 dromedaries**.  
